  "instruction": "What's the bus route in Halifax that goes along Oxford and ends over at the terminal by the Walmart and Sobeys?",
  "answer": "**Route 1 Spring Garden** is the Halifax Transit bus route that runs along Oxford Street and terminates at **Mumford Terminal** — the transit terminal located right next to the Walmart and Sobeys at the Halifax Shopping Centre on Mumford Road.\n\n## Verification from official sources\n\n**Route 1 Spring Garden runs the full length of Oxford Street** in both directions per Halifax Transit's official route descriptions:\n- **Bridge Terminal → Mumford Terminal**: \"...continue on Coburg Road, **right on Oxford Street**, left on Almon Street... continue to *Mumford Terminal Bay 2*\"\n- **Mumford Terminal → Bridge Terminal**: \"Depart *Mumford Terminal Bay 2*... **right on Oxford Street**, left on Coburg Road...\" [1]\n\n**Mumford Terminal location**: Situated at 7010 Mumford Road in the Halifax Shopping Centre complex. Both Walmart (6990 Mumford Rd) and Sobeys (6990 Mumford Rd, West End Mall) are directly adjacent to the terminal — all three share the same mall complex [2, 3].\n\n**Route 1 is currently active** as a \"Corridor Route\" offering frequent daily service (including evenings/weekends) in the official August 2026 route list [4].\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] https://www.halifax.ca/transportation/halifax-transit/routes-schedules/route-descriptions  \n[2] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halifax_Shopping_Centre  \n[3] https://www.sobeys.com/stores/sobeys-mumford-road  \n[4] https://www.halifax.ca/transportation/halifax-transit/routes-schedules",
